  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f424be585f9e04c79a96c8292e8b9db1, type: 3}
  m_Name: Chefe_BigTech
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Metis.Runtime::KnowledgeEntryData
  _title: Cidades inteligentes e dados dos moradores
  _titleEn: Smart cities and residents' data
  _category: 2
  _unlockTrigger: 14
  _summary: "Empresas de tecnologia oferecem sensores, aplicativos e plataformas
    para administrar a cidade. Em troca, ficam com os dados de quem mora nela, sob
    termos de uso que quase ningu\xE9m l\xEA. O pesquisador Ben Green defende uma
    cidade inteligente o bastante, que usa tecnologia s\xF3 onde ela resolve um problema
    real."
  _summaryEn: Tech companies offer sensors, apps and platforms to run the city. In
    return, they keep the data of the people who live there, under terms of service
    almost nobody reads. Researcher Ben Green argues for a smart enough city, one
    that uses technology only where it solves a real problem.
  _realWorld: "Em Toronto, a Sidewalk Labs, empresa do mesmo grupo do Google, planejou
    o bairro de Quayside cheio de sensores. Em outubro de 2018, Ann Cavoukian, ex-comiss\xE1ria
    de privacidade de Ont\xE1rio, deixou o projeto porque a anonimiza\xE7\xE3o dos
    dados seria s\xF3 incentivada, n\xE3o exigida. Em maio de 2020, a empresa desistiu."
  _realWorldEn: In Toronto, Sidewalk Labs, a sister company of Google, planned the
    Quayside district full of sensors. In October 2018, Ann Cavoukian, Ontario's
    former privacy commissioner, left the project because anonymizing the data would
    only be encouraged, not required. In May 2020, the company pulled out.
  _tradeOffs: "A parceria traz investimento e servi\xE7os novos sem custo imediato
    para a prefeitura. O pre\xE7o aparece depois: depend\xEAncia de um fornecedor,
    perda de controle sobre os dados e decis\xF5es p\xFAblicas tomadas por uma empresa."
  _tradeOffsEn: 'The partnership brings investment and new services at no upfront
    cost to City Hall. The price shows up later: dependence on one vendor, loss of
    control over the data and public decisions made by a company.'
  _sources:
  - Label: The Globe and Mail, Privacy expert Ann Cavoukian resigns from Sidewalk
      Toronto (2018)
    Url: https://theglobeandmail.com/business/article-privacy-expert-ann-cavoukian-resigns-from-sidewalk-toronto-smart-city/
  - Label: Osgoode Hall Law School (IPOsgoode), Sidewalk Labs withdraws from Quayside
      development project (2020)
    Url: https://www.yorku.ca/osgoode/iposgoode/2020/05/21/sidewalk-labs-withdraws-from-quayside-development-project/
  - Label: New Books Network, Ben Green, The Smart Enough City (MIT Press, 2019)
    Url: https://newbooksnetwork.com/ben-green-the-smart-enough-city-putting-technology-in-its-place-to-reclaim-our-urban-future-mit-press-2019
